This repository holds two kinds of code, and only one of them is licensed.

COVERED by the first MIT License below -- the project's original work:

  * the run.sh script and the repository's other top-level files;
  * the files under src/, tools/, scripts/ and docker/ marked ORIGINAL in
    PROVENANCE.tsv (the PVR renderer, the asset and disc
    layer, the AICA synthesiser, the memory-card code, the debug probes,
    the host test harness, the build files, the asset exporters and the
    checks), and those directories' files the table does not list;
  * the port's own code inside the files marked MIXED there.

NOT COVERED -- no license is granted for it by this project:

  * the files marked DERIVED or SGI in that table, and the
    decomp-derived functions and tables inside the MIXED files. They are
    ported from, or copied out of, the ssb-decomp-re decompilation
    (https://github.com/VetriTheRetri/ssb-decomp-re), which declares no
    license, and through it from Nintendo's Super Smash Bros. and Silicon
    Graphics' libultra. This project cannot grant rights it does not hold.
  * the game itself. No ROM, asset or other game data is distributed
    here; building needs your own legally obtained copy.

COVERED by the second MIT License below (Team Resurgent) -- the Xbox
port's original work:

  * the files under Platform/xbox/ marked ORIGINAL in PROVENANCE.tsv, and
    the port's own code inside the files marked KOS there;
  * tools/xbox/, setup.py, build.bat, rxdk.project.json, SSB-X.sln, SSB-X.vcxproj(.filters)
    and .gitattributes;
  * the Xbox port's changes marked XBOX: in the files under src/ and tools/.

Under the KOS License, NOT the MIT terms: the KallistiOS code carried into
the files marked KOS in PROVENANCE.tsv (see Platform/xbox/LICENSE.KOS).

